## Agent contract

`AGENTS.md` is the canonical operating contract. `CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md`
only direct their agents to it through vendor-specific discovery filenames.
Keep shared rules in `AGENTS.md` rather than duplicating them in adapters or
this README.

## Directory contract

| Directory | What belongs there |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/` | Current durable project knowledge |
| `planning/` | Forward plans only when coordination, risk, or duration justifies one |
| `handoffs/` | State crossing a real session, agent, model, operator, repository, or workspace boundary |
| `scripts/` | Stable, narrow operations with explicit inputs and bounded effects |
| `swarms/` | Optional multi-agent task manifests and executable checks |
| `temp/` | Disposable scratch files and worktrees; never commit |
| `.agent/` | Live continuity and replaceable agent state; never commit |

Application directories and project-specific rules should develop from the
project's actual needs.
